{"name":"Dollar Bill","hex":"#85bb65","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dollar bill","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A note of currency worth one dollar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dollar_bill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dollar Bill (Jack White song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Dollar Bill\" is a song by the American musician Jack White, released as the second single from his seventh studio album Frozen Charlotte (2026) on June 10, 2026. It was announced via a 30-second preview upload to a channel named \"The Frozen Charlatan\", with the video simply titled \"$$$\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dollar_Bill_(Jack_White_song)","wikidata":"Q141659258"},{"title":"Dollar","blocks":[{"text":"Dollar is the name of more than 25 currencies and their base units. The United States dollar, named after the international currency known as the Spanish dollar, was established in 1792 and is the first so named that still survives. Others include the Australian dollar, Brunei dollar, Canadian dollar, Eastern Caribbean dollar, Hong Kong dollar, Jamaican dollar, Liberian dollar, Namibian dollar, New Taiwan dollar, New Zealand dollar, Singapore dollar, Trinidad and Tobago dollar, and several others. The symbol for most of those currencies is the dollar sign $; the same symbol is used by many countries using peso currencies."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/Joachimsthaler_1525.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dollar","wikidata":"Q14083"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Joachimsthaler_1525.jpg/250px-Joachimsthaler_1525.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/Joachimsthaler_1525.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://